    "mahalaya": {
      "date": "2026-10-10",
      "dateLabel": "Saturday, October 10, 2026",
      "tithi": "Ashwina Amavasya",
      "title": "Mahalaya — মহালয়া",
      "significance": "End of Pitru Paksha and the eve of Devi Paksha — the day Bengalis invoke Maa Durga with 'Ya Devi Sarvabhuteshu' and begin the festive fortnight. Note: some Houston organizers (e.g. HDBS) observe Mahalaya on Oct 11; panchang Amavasya is Oct 10.",
      "mahishasuramardini": "Since 1931, All India Radio has broadcast Birendra Krishna Bhadra's Mahishasuramardini — Chandipath and songs — at 4 AM on Mahalaya morning. SDKKM celebrates with a community Mahishasuramardini singing program at 11 AM.",
      "tarpan": "Til Tarpan for ancestors is offered on Mahalaya morning — HDBS holds Til Tarpan 7:00–9:30 AM on Oct 10."
    },
    "sourceNote": "Houston organizers: Houston Durga Bari Society (durgabari.org), Maitri in Houston (maitri-houston.org), Shiv Durga Krishna Kali Mandir (sdkkm.org), Vedanta Society of Greater Houston (houstonvedanta.org), Houston Kali Temple (houstonkalitemple.org). Unlike the Bay Area, Houston's big pujas (HDBS, SDKKM) follow the actual tithi calendar — Shashthi through Dashami, Oct 15–20 — rather than weekends. Schedules change — always confirm with the organizer before traveling."
  },
